# Tracer: standard numeric-set membership hierarchy
#
# Before (Litex verified, but compiler emission stopped):
# forall n N:
#     n $in Z
# Former compiler behavior: fail closed at
# `Builtin(StandardSetMembershipProjection)`.
#
# Now: the compiler validates the exact source and target standard sets and
# replays only the native-carrier hierarchy N -> Z -> Q -> R -> C. The source
# value keeps its original Lean carrier and independent Litex.In evidence.
forall n N:
    n $in Z

forall n N:
    n $in Q

forall n N:
    n $in R

forall n N:
    n $in C

forall z Z:
    z $in Q

forall z Z:
    z $in R

forall z Z:
    z $in C

forall q Q:
    q $in R

forall q Q:
    q $in C

forall r R:
    r $in C

# Boundary (Litex verifies; compiler remains fail-closed):
# forall n N+:
#     n $in N
# The verifier uses the same hierarchy certificate, but N+ has a refined
# exact carrier whose native compiler ABI has not yet been implemented. This
# batch must not erase its positivity predicate or treat it as plain N.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/16_StandardSetHierarchy.lit
# cargo test --release --test litex_to_lean_compiler_tracers standard_set_hierarchy
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples
